WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.890
Ice keeps its shape.

2
00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:03.450
Water does not.

3
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.530
Pour it, and it takes
the shape of its cup.

4
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:09.710
Steam spreads out to fill
its whole container.

5
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.970
Three very different things.

6
00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:16.110
Yet ice, water and steam are
made of the same particles.

7
00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:18.030
Not one of them is new.

8
00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.570
So why do they behave so differently?

9
00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.810
Do the particles themselves change?

10
00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:24.610
Or is it something else?

11
00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:27.930
In this mission, you'll
meet the particle model.

12
00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:30.690
You'll look inside a
solid, a liquid and a gas,

13
00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:33.930
and find out which
one can be squashed.

14
00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:38.910
Your mission: explain why ice,
water and steam are so different.
